title: Vesting incentive for validator self-stake

doc:
- audience: Runtime Dev
  description: |-
    Extend the `vesting` and `staking-async` pallets to deliver validator self-stake
    incentives as vested payouts (issue #11876) instead of liquid transfers. Each account's
    vesting schedule space is partitioned between distinct schedule origins. Vested
    transfers that cannot be accommodated into any schedule get dropped (no liquid fallback).

    ## Changes to `pallet-vesting`:

    - A new `VestedPayout` trait allows the addition of new vesting schedules either as new
      entries or through merging with existing schedules that start at the same block
    - A new `VestingKind` enum that differentiates the vesting schedule origins (currently
      supporting `Public` and `System`) and which is used to partition the vesting schedule
      capacity, with merging allowed only for schedules from the same origin
    - All existing schedules are tagged as `Public` so a V1 → V2 migration is needed

    ## Changes to `pallet-staking-async`:

    - New `Config` items that define how vesting schedules execute (`VestingBondingPeriods`,
      `BlocksPerSession`, `VestingBlockNumberProvider` and `ValidatorIncentivePayout`)
    - The `VestingEpochStartBlocks` map correlates bonding-period windows (past or present)
      with unique start blocks that are used for same-origin vesting schedule merging


